# Express API

Mount routers in `app.ts` under `/api/v1`. Route files only register middleware and controllers.

Session:

- `POST /api/v1/session` accepts `{ token }`, checks it with upstream `GET /instance/status`, and sets an `HttpOnly` cookie. The JSON body must not echo the token.
- `DELETE /api/v1/session` clears the cookie.

Instance (cookie required): `status`, `connect`, `qr`, `pair`, `reconnect`, `disconnect`. Map them to the allowed upstream routes in `product.mdc`. Reject anything else with the normal error envelope.

- Protected order: `requireInstanceSession -> validateRequest -> controller`.
- `POST /session` is public and still validated.
- Controllers read validated input, call one application service, and map the result to HTTP.
- Success with a body: `{ success: true, data }`. Failure: `{ success: false, error: { code, message } }`.
- `204` has no body.
- Call `next(error)` into the centralized error handler. Register `404`, then `errorMiddleware` last in `app.ts`.
- Status codes: `200`, `204`, `400`, `401`, `422`, `502`, `503`. Upstream failures become `502` with a generic message.
